    {
      "id": "claim_d347e618477d42cc9c9585decd48213d",
      "statement": "RaindropService.saveToRaindrop validates integration configuration (not-configured, disabled, no collection selected) and throws IllegalStateException or IllegalArgumentException before ever invoking RaindropApiClient, so business-rule validation runs outside the circuit breaker.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/integration/RaindropService.java#L32-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a7636112756c3bee18f5619caca65252276cb4029dfec961411ada1de38320fd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3ce9d2817a1440e39c92a2941aba7214",
      "statement": "RaindropApiClientImpl is a separate Spring bean from RaindropService carrying @CircuitBreaker(name = \"raindrop\") and @Retry(name = \"raindrop\") on listCollections and createBookmark, avoiding the AOP self-invocation trap where annotations on a method called from within the same bean would bypass the proxy.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/integration/RaindropApiClientImpl.java#L14-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b4b89cd8b39a3ea9a71b1f1427758da7de757955260ae0c25d2ebc2a641b40e2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_70ba431de3ce4cdb93619f0ee89786fe",
      "statement": "RaindropApiClientImpl's fallback methods (listCollectionsFallback, createBookmarkFallback) explicitly check for RaindropNotConfiguredException and rethrow it unchanged so it reaches GlobalExceptionHandler as a 503; any other throwable is wrapped as IllegalStateException(\"Raindrop.io is currently unavailable\") mapped to 409.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/integration/RaindropApiClientImpl.java#L68-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc8a16de91f5fae8e68ed204f9fec99585fe0522116fb80cb311b80c998cd603:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2384afb830e6437caf32565f1b987757",
      "statement": "RaindropApiClientImpl.requireConfigured throws RaindropNotConfiguredException whenever the configured apiToken is null or blank, and this exception type must be listed under ignore-exceptions for both the raindrop circuit breaker and retry instances so an unconfigured token never opens the breaker or burns retry attempts.",
