    {
      "id": "claim_8bc55c3e86374da7a18e96a260d5d742",
      "statement": "After RaindropApiClient.createBookmark returns successfully, RaindropService.saveToRaindrop calls ArticleEngagementStore.recordQuietly(article.getId(), EngagementKind.RAINDROP) to record a RAINDROP engagement, placed after the breaker-wrapped call so a blocked or failed save (breaker open, retries exhausted, not-configured) never records an engagement.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/integration/RaindropService.java#L27-L54",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:88bf53c14fa897d9404d022b4841ae61eb3ce2e488fde17c5139a72bad9a0559:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c007629396cd455f8c70ad3f66fb827c",
      "statement": "ArticleEngagementStore opens no transaction: record/recordQuietly issue a single autocommitting INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING statement, and recordQuietly catches DataAccessException and logs a WARN instead of propagating, so a failed RAINDROP engagement insert can never abort or roll back the user's Raindrop.io save.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/repository/ArticleEngagementStore.java#L12-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ecabf3fd87e44e201d4c94a106f518f8a5c48a992f6cc4a6fca33ff688be0e05:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_52d4adfd74bb4d56b85c91a02cb228b8",
      "statement": "The RaindropService/RaindropApiClientImpl split (business validation outside the breaker, @CircuitBreaker/@Retry on a separate client bean) is the general convention for external integrations in myfeeder and is reused by the newer Jev/TypeSafe integration (JevApiClientImpl carries @CircuitBreaker(name = \"jev\") + @Retry(name = \"jev\")) with its own breaker name and tuning.",
